  "@type": "SoftwareSourceCode",
  "name": "TriAgent",
  "description": "TriAgent is a divergence-aware multi-agent routing framework that reduces large language model inference cost by routing each query to the cheapest model tier that can answer it correctly. It stratifies agents by contextual granularity - a word-level lexicon, a sentence-level domain transformer, and a cross-sentence LLM reasoner - and uses the Semantic Divergence Index (SDI), the pairwise disagreement between those tiers, as an unsupervised routing signal, a multilingual semantic cache key, and a post-hoc LLM hallucination detector at AUC 0.90.",
